// ScholarPi Assessment Circuit
// Proves a manuscript passed assessment without revealing the exact scores on-chain.

// Arguments:
// 1. vapri (private): The calculated score from your Python backend.
// 2. threshold (private): The minimum score required to pass.
// 3. truncatedHashInt (public): Binds this proof to the specific manuscript hash.

def main(private field vapri, private field threshold, field truncatedHashInt) {
    
    // Assert that the manuscript's score meets or exceeds the required threshold
    assert(vapri >= threshold);
    
    // The circuit successfully completes. 
    // Because truncatedHashInt is the only non-private argument, 
    // it becomes the single public input expected by your smart contract.
    return;
}